From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:55:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 025/147] mobile: in touch mode a finger left from a pinch does
 not drag

Since "a gesture is over once its fingers lift", the finger left on the glass
after a pinch becomes a one-finger pan about 200 ms after the other one
lifted. In mouse mode that moves the cursor, as intended. In touch mode a
one-finger pan is a left-button drag on the PC: ending a zoom with a trailing
finger that kept moving could drag a file or a window, or select text; if
the pinch began less than 500 ms before, the press went to the first touch
point. In 1.5.0 that finger kept panning the local canvas.

In touch mode such a finger is now ignored until every finger has lifted:
onTwoFingerScaleEnd notes that a finger is still down, the one-finger pan
then sends no press and moves no cursor, and onLongPressDown, which runs for
the first finger of every touch, clears the note. Its lift still sends the
spare button release a pinch already ends with. Mouse mode is unchanged;
desktop touch screens, which take the touch path, get the same fix.

No unit test: the handlers need a session's models. The review's gesture
probe (makeGestures' recognizers with these handlers, mouse and touch mode)
shows the drag gone and every other scenario unchanged.

(Release 1.5.1 review, dart-behavior "missed" item 1.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
